(5973893, 871749, 10785, '<td valign="top">Good B&amp;W Conversion here. Overall the shot is pretty mundane without much interest... the flat field leading to a distant brush edge reveails no interesting land shapes or objects. One compositional rule to think about is the rule of thirds. Here your horizon line is at about the halfway mark in the photo. Try using one of the thirds to line up the horizon, either the top or bottom. Also the tree on the left doesn''t really frame anything. If you could get that in the shot in one of left most third then that would add some interest. I have a nice link to some articles on composition that have helped me out... <a href="//photoinf.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//photoinf.com</a></td>', 'Good B&W Conversion here. Overall the shot is pretty mundane without much interest... the flat field leading to a distant brush edge reveails no interesting land shapes or objects. One compositional rule to think about is the rule of thirds. Here your horizon line is at about the halfway mark in the photo. Try using one of the thirds to line up the horizon, either the top or bottom. Also the tree on the left doesn''t really frame anything. If you could get that in the shot in one of left most third then that would add some interest. I have a nice link to some articles on composition that have helped me out... //photoinf.com', '2010-04-27 10:16:16.000000', NULL, 1),
