(5984278, 874124, 81362, '<td valign="top">My top pick of the urban entries. Wonderful that the brightness of the traffic flow becomes nearly uniform in contrast to the windows/twinkles in the darker buildings and the smooth sky.</td>', 'My top pick of the urban entries. Wonderful that the brightness of the traffic flow becomes nearly uniform in contrast to the windows/twinkles in the darker buildings and the smooth sky.', '2010-05-02 11:11:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984280, 873994, 81362, '<td valign="top">I find it easy to enjoy the strong contrast between the dark "islands" in clouds while there is still just a hint of detail in the more distant hills.</td>', 'I find it easy to enjoy the strong contrast between the dark "islands" in clouds while there is still just a hint of detail in the more distant hills.', '2010-05-02 11:13:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984302, 874228, 64086, '<td valign="top">Really great photo and mood. I think I would have cropped out the moon. It  is so small and appears misshapen which detracts from the nice composition.</td>', 'Really great photo and mood. I think I would have cropped out the moon. It  is so small and appears misshapen which detracts from the nice composition.', '2010-05-02 11:22:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984305, 873790, 64086, '<td valign="top">Wow! The light is really beautiful.</td>', 'Wow! The light is really beautiful.', '2010-05-02 11:24:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984316, 874026, 103142, '<td valign="top">I have a few problems with the composition of this shot. The trees hold the most interest in the shot, but they''re not very interesting. I think I would have liked it cropped in a bit more to bring the focus on the bridge. I''m also wondering whether it would have been more interesting seeing the creek or depression that the bridge is spanning instead of the trees to the side.<br/> <br/>Last thought -- did you try flipping the image horizontally? Sometimes having the subject on the left gives it a little more prominence and draws the eye more.<br/> <br/>(edited to change it to subject on left instead of right!)</td>', 'I have a few problems with the composition of this shot. The trees hold the most interest in the shot, but they''re not very interesting. I think I would have liked it cropped in a bit more to bring the focus on the bridge. I''m also wondering whether it would have been more interesting seeing the creek or depression that the bridge is spanning instead of the trees to the side. Last thought -- did you try flipping the image horizontally? Sometimes having the subject on the left gives it a little more prominence and draws the eye more. (edited to change it to subject on left instead of right!)', '2010-05-02 11:37:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984319, 874112, 12674, '<td valign="top">It feels more about sky than the fields. A landscape orientation might''ve emphasized the fields more.</td>', 'It feels more about sky than the fields. A landscape orientation might''ve emphasized the fields more.', '2010-05-02 11:40:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984323, 874026, 12674, '<td valign="top">Pretty setting. I wouldn''t have known it was a covered bridge. A different angle or perspective to reveal more of the stream it is crossing might''ve been helpful.</td>', 'Pretty setting. I wouldn''t have known it was a covered bridge. A different angle or perspective to reveal more of the stream it is crossing might''ve been helpful.', '2010-05-02 11:45:22.000000', NULL, 1),
