(5987538, 874261, 57202, '<td valign="top">Thanks, Jeb!  This spot is actually about 20 minutes away from my place up in Idyllwild.  It had snowed all night and I knew I had to shoot it before I headed to work. :)  N.T.F.S.?</td>', 'Thanks, Jeb!  This spot is actually about 20 minutes away from my place up in Idyllwild.  It had snowed all night and I knew I had to shoot it before I headed to work. :)  N.T.F.S.?', '2010-05-03 12:21:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5987556, 872945, 35804, '<td valign="top">For the life of me, I can''t figure out why so many see this as blown out/over exposed. I can''t! Or maybe people weren''t using the proper terminology? Perhaps "pale" might have been a better term...but then again, "pale" is not a flaw...and one must always seek the flaw when looking at a photograph.<br/> <br/>...or, maybe some serious monitor calibrations are in order for some of the viewing/voting population.</td>', 'For the life of me, I can''t figure out why so many see this as blown out/over exposed. I can''t! Or maybe people weren''t using the proper terminology? Perhaps "pale" might have been a better term...but then again, "pale" is not a flaw...and one must always seek the flaw when looking at a photograph. ...or, maybe some serious monitor calibrations are in order for some of the viewing/voting population.', '2010-05-03 12:27:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5987559, 873812, 67258, '<td valign="top">I have to admit I am fairly ambivalent about this photo - I don''t think this standard view of seeing the landscape suits your eye, photo vision, style.  I far prefer your street work, urban landscapes, and quirky urban landscape details.</td>', 'I have to admit I am fairly ambivalent about this photo - I don''t think this standard view of seeing the landscape suits your eye, photo vision, style.  I far prefer your street work, urban landscapes, and quirky urban landscape details.', '2010-05-03 12:29:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5987567, 872548, 92847, '<td valign="top">Greg, congrats on the well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'Greg, congrats on the well deserved ribbon!', '2010-05-03 12:33:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5987569, 873647, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by northebound:</b></div><hr/><i> Ugh - I WISH this photo was larger. And, in this way, I think the border hurts you a little bit, because all the beautiful details (water drops and plants) are scrunched due to the limit of resolution. I don''t hate the border - just don''t feel it works in this photo - particularly this photo online. I would love to see a full version of this. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>See, I disagree with "the limit of resolution".  The image may have worked best at this aspect ratio/crop.  Maybe there wasn''t anything of interest above or below what''s presented.  By using the full 800px in width nothing really was lost in the details.<br/> <br/>I agree that the border doesn''t help with the dark tones...although it may have worked with just a one pixel grey line between the image and the letterbox.  ???<br/> <br/>Lovely image BTW - I gave it a 7.</td>', 'Originally posted by northebound: Ugh - I WISH this photo was larger. And, in this way, I think the border hurts you a little bit, because all the beautiful details (water drops and plants) are scrunched due to the limit of resolution. I don''t hate the border - just don''t feel it works in this photo - particularly this photo online. I would love to see a full version of this.  See, I disagree with "the limit of resolution".  The image may have worked best at this aspect ratio/crop.  Maybe there wasn''t anything of interest above or below what''s presented.  By using the full 800px in width nothing really was lost in the details. I agree that the border doesn''t help with the dark tones...although it may have worked with just a one pixel grey line between the image and the letterbox.  ??? Lovely image BTW - I gave it a 7.', '2010-05-03 12:33:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5987571, 873405, 67258, '<td valign="top">I was one of your lower votes, and spent some time viewing the photo before I voted.  On balance, I found the ultra low viewpoint unsettling, and initially found it hard to make sense of the scene.  The sense of drama and the tonal range are good, although I wonder if the blacks could have been pushed a little more?</td>', 'I was one of your lower votes, and spent some time viewing the photo before I voted.  On balance, I found the ultra low viewpoint unsettling, and initially found it hard to make sense of the scene.  The sense of drama and the tonal range are good, although I wonder if the blacks could have been pushed a little more?', '2010-05-03 12:34:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5987572, 873405, 67258, '<td valign="top">I was one of your lower votes, and spent some time viewing the photo before I voted.  On balance, I found the ultra low viewpoint unsettling, and initially found it hard to make sense of the scene.  The sense of drama and the tonal range are good, although I wonder if the blacks could have been pushed a little more?</td>', 'I was one of your lower votes, and spent some time viewing the photo before I voted.  On balance, I found the ultra low viewpoint unsettling, and initially found it hard to make sense of the scene.  The sense of drama and the tonal range are good, although I wonder if the blacks could have been pushed a little more?', '2010-05-03 12:34:08.000000', NULL, 0),
