(6013521, 874303, 67152, '<td valign="top">The scene itself is serene, but the location really does not draw us in or make us want to linger. The light is harsh (as if taken mid afternoon). You would be better to back and visit this spot late in the afternoon or early in the morning to get the rich soft light on the trees. <br/> <br/>You also have some significant processing issues - blown out clouds, muddy sky, blurry details.</td>', 'The scene itself is serene, but the location really does not draw us in or make us want to linger. The light is harsh (as if taken mid afternoon). You would be better to back and visit this spot late in the afternoon or early in the morning to get the rich soft light on the trees.  You also have some significant processing issues - blown out clouds, muddy sky, blurry details.', '2010-05-18 20:10:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6015642, 874303, 49109, '<td valign="top">Light is coming from the wrong side here, leading to a dark bridge without details and blown out clouds. Besides that there are JPG-artefacts in the sky.</td>', 'Light is coming from the wrong side here, leading to a dark bridge without details and blown out clouds. Besides that there are JPG-artefacts in the sky.', '2010-05-19 10:21:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6015775, 874303, 113419, '<td valign="top">Again, I can''t be of much help as black and white landscape just blew my mind.  When I shot for this I had to keep telling myself - black and white used to be all you could shoot in and folks back when did some stunning work.  I do however see that I gave you a 4 on this and that is the lowest I will score anyone.<br/>What I''m seeing is very blown out clouds.  I think maybe you shot this around noon? (or noonish)  That''s a really hard time to shoot cause the sun is so harsh at that time of day.  And mostly that''s where my eyes land when I look at this image so I really don''t see the rest of it.  I took a piece of paper and "cropped" out about 3/4 of the sky and that really, (imho) helped the image alot.  I think it toned it down and gave it more contrast.<br/>Anyway, I hope this helps.  Now GO BEAT SPIFF!</td>', 'Again, I can''t be of much help as black and white landscape just blew my mind.  When I shot for this I had to keep telling myself - black and white used to be all you could shoot in and folks back when did some stunning work.  I do however see that I gave you a 4 on this and that is the lowest I will score anyone.What I''m seeing is very blown out clouds.  I think maybe you shot this around noon? (or noonish)  That''s a really hard time to shoot cause the sun is so harsh at that time of day.  And mostly that''s where my eyes land when I look at this image so I really don''t see the rest of it.  I took a piece of paper and "cropped" out about 3/4 of the sky and that really, (imho) helped the image alot.  I think it toned it down and gave it more contrast.Anyway, I hope this helps.  Now GO BEAT SPIFF!', '2010-05-19 11:01:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6023567, 872278, 54645, '<td valign="top">Wonderful textures and light.</td>', 'Wonderful textures and light.', '2010-05-24 04:04:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6029223, 873903, 17507, '<td valign="top">Great choice of subject for this challenge, and nicely framed. You''ve done a lovely job of bringing out the full tonal range, and the effect is striking. As some voters suggested, you might have toned it down a bit, but that''s largely a matter of taste.<br/> <br/>In the realm of constructive criticism, I have a couple of things to offer perhaps for next time:<br/> <br/>- The focus looks a little soft. I don''t know if this was intentional, but I see that "Sharpen" is in your PP notes. Do you ever use Unsharp Mask? I find it does a much better job about 99% of the time. Try a radius of .3 to .5 pixels with a threshold of 0.<br/> <br/>- The white lines on the cinema-style border are a bit bright. A more neutral gray would have had the same effect without drawing the eye out of the frame.<br/> <br/>A solid entry in a difficult challenge! Looking forward to seeing more landscapes from you.</td>', 'Great choice of subject for this challenge, and nicely framed. You''ve done a lovely job of bringing out the full tonal range, and the effect is striking. As some voters suggested, you might have toned it down a bit, but that''s largely a matter of taste. In the realm of constructive criticism, I have a couple of things to offer perhaps for next time: - The focus looks a little soft. I don''t know if this was intentional, but I see that "Sharpen" is in your PP notes. Do you ever use Unsharp Mask? I find it does a much better job about 99% of the time. Try a radius of .3 to .5 pixels with a threshold of 0. - The white lines on the cinema-style border are a bit bright. A more neutral gray would have had the same effect without drawing the eye out of the frame. A solid entry in a difficult challenge! Looking forward to seeing more landscapes from you.', '2010-05-26 23:26:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6033457, 873994, 46314, '<td valign="top">Nice shot - well processed. Looks like a stunning location.</td>', 'Nice shot - well processed. Looks like a stunning location.', '2010-05-31 10:40:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6066680, 873820, 114285, '<td valign="top">Nice</td>', 'Nice', '2010-06-23 00:29:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6074933, 872066, 55822, '<td valign="top">This is a fantastic shot, the depth draws me into the scene, wanting more. The relationship between the wood in the foreground and background leave me wondering if they were at some point in time attatched to one another. The B&amp;W conversion here is beautiful, rich range of tones. I do have to agree with [user]Bear Music[/user] that the inline boarder hurts the overall impact, however not much.</td>', 'This is a fantastic shot, the depth draws me into the scene, wanting more. The relationship between the wood in the foreground and background leave me wondering if they were at some point in time attatched to one another. The B&W conversion here is beautiful, rich range of tones. I do have to agree with [user]Bear Music[/user] that the inline boarder hurts the overall impact, however not much.', '2010-06-30 22:04:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6077230, 872866, 97270, '<td valign="top">Love the perspective, and the leading lines. B&amp;W helps too. A little but of contrast adjustment may have brought the details in trees up, and a slightly tighter crop at the bottom could do wonders so one of the lines would meet the corner perfectly.<br/> <br/>Good job!<br/> <br/>[<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1014133" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Game: Comment or Die!</a>]</td>', 'Love the perspective, and the leading lines. B&W helps too. A little but of contrast adjustment may have brought the details in trees up, and a slightly tighter crop at the bottom could do wonders so one of the lines would meet the corner perfectly. Good job! [Game: Comment or Die!]', '2010-07-02 12:27:57.000000', NULL, 0),
